    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0148" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg44"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Mizner.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-08-04"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 4,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wharton informs Mr. Ryan of the receipt of Mr. Mizner’s telegram of the 1st
                    instant, through the legation in Mexico, and instructs him to telegraph Mr.
                    Mizner that the Department considers it necessary for him to go to San José and
                    place himself in communication with the Government of Salvador through the
                    United States naval vessels at that port, as well as with the Guatemalan
                    Government, in order that he may offer his good offices to both countries.</p>
            </div>
